<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>GoBuiltinFunctions - Tag - loommii</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gobuiltinfunctions/</link><description>我的个人技术博客</description><generator>Hugo 0.165.0 &amp; FixIt v0.4.5</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 16 Jan 2026 01:28:43 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://loommii.github.io/en/tags/gobuiltinfunctions/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Go Daily Question 139</title><link>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_139/</link><pubDate>Mon, 23 Dec 2024 17:01:49 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://loommii.github.io/en/go_practise/go_daily_question_139/</guid><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/godailyquestion/">GoDailyQuestion</category><category domain="https://loommii.github.io/en/categories/golanguagebasics/">GoLanguageBasics</category><description>&lt;p&gt;Which of the following types can use the &lt;code&gt;cap()&lt;/code&gt; function?&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;A. array&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;B. slice&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;C. map&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;D. channel&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;details&gt;&#10; &lt;summary&gt;🔑 Answer Analysis:&lt;/summary&gt;&#10; &lt;p&gt;ABD&#10;&lt;a href="https://pkg.go.dev/builtin#cap" target="_blank" rel="external nofollow noopener noreferrer"&gt;Official documentation&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;pre&gt;&lt;code&gt;func cap(v Type) int&#10;// The built-in function `cap` returns the capacity of `v` based on its type:&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Array: the number of elements in &lt;code&gt;v&lt;/code&gt; (same as &lt;code&gt;len(v)&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Pointer to array &lt;code&gt;*array&lt;/code&gt;: the number of elements in &lt;code&gt;*v&lt;/code&gt; (same as &lt;code&gt;len(v)&lt;/code&gt;).&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Slice: the maximum length the slice can reach when re-sliced;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Channel: the buffer capacity of the channel, in terms of elements;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;If &lt;code&gt;v&lt;/code&gt; is &lt;code&gt;nil&lt;/code&gt;, then &lt;code&gt;cap(v)&lt;/code&gt; is zero.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;/details&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>